**What this session established.** Picking up from sess306's verified P283 fix, the plan of record's next work on the #1 critical defect (D-FOREIGN-REPLAY-UNGATED-IMAGES) is build-order **step 6: F1 deferred-release enforcement** — the first step that changes behavior rather than adding telemetry. I audited both release classes and confirmed the enforcement gaps precisely: the ICLUS path CASes unconditionally even when the settle timed out, the keyed proof failed, or the pre-CAS tripwire fired (`mxfs_iclus_disk_release`, CAS at xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:47355), its retry substrate is event-driven only (no self-rescheduling worker, no admission closure between deferred attempts), and the relbar proof-failed exit (14948) still proceeds to CAS. All three F*_READY constants remain 0.

**RULE-5 ruling obtained** and recorded (ccmemory `ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess307-GPT-ruling-step6-F1-deferred-release-enforcement`, also appended to the ledger). Key decisions: defer on {still_dirty, proof_failed, tripwire} but not the F2/NO_DOMAIN case; a single load-time knob `release_proof_enforce` defaulting to 1; a per-cluster self-rescheduling worker with a release_epoch ABA guard; admission closure during deferred DEMOTING (entered at first deferral, preserving the MHT tenure-floor batching — a documented adaptation); wall-clock wedge bounds (60s no-progress / 300s total) with a one-shot forced shutdown and the wedged grant pinned out of teardown's release_all; the -EDEADLK selfclear escape gets no exemption; and the relbar proof-failed exit flips to the existing strand/dwork channel. The ruling also flagged hazards (drain deadlock, flush storms, unmount/worker lifetime) that the implementation checklist now carries.

Ledger and handoff are updated with the full implementation map and verification plan (board green first, then fault-injection to assert defer-instead-of-CAS). Criteria not met — 36 defects remain open (24 critical); no YES marker written.

